     ],
     "value": "Highly expressed in the liver and, at lower levels, in skeletal muscle, including in vastus lateralis, gastrocnemius and soleus (at protein level). Highest mRNA levels are observed in skeletal muscle, and only moderate levels in liver and heart. Weak expression in placenta and lung"
    }
   ],
   "commentType": "TISSUE SPECIFICITY"
  },
  {
   "texts": [
    {
     "evidences": [
      {
       "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250"
      }
     ],
     "value": "The N-terminal region is required for binding to PP1, the central region is required for binding to glycogen and the C-terminal region is required for binding to PYGL"
    }
   ],
   "commentType": "DOMAIN"
  }
